<!-- ===== Why Physical Verification Matters ===== -->
<section class="section statement why-physical">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal">Why physical verification matters</span>
    <h2 class="display-md reveal mt-3">More design possibilities create<br>a greater need for physical evidence.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="container why-physical__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="measure reveal why-physical__p">AI and digital design tools are making it faster to generate, visualize, and revise ideas. But producing more options does not necessarily make the right decision clearer.</p>
      <p class="measure reveal mt-3 why-physical__p">Before a design moves into approval, fabrication, construction, or production, teams still need to understand how it works in physical space—its scale, proportion, relationships, materials, assembly, and effect on the people who experience it.</p>
      <p class="measure reveal mt-3 why-physical__p">A physical model gives teams something tangible to examine together. It helps make complex ideas easier to understand, reveals questions that may be missed on a screen, and builds confidence before committing to the next stage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-physical__visual reveal">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <div class="why-physical__placeholder">
        <span>Side-by-side comparison — physical model vs. Revit digital model</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

