<!-- ===== FAQ teaser ===== -->
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal">Common questions</span>
    <h2 class="display-md reveal mt-3">Good to know.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How much does a physical model cost? <span class="pm"></span></summary>
        <p>Carve Model projects start at US$4,000. Final pricing depends on the model's size, scale, level of detail, source information, materials, features, schedule, packaging, and delivery requirements.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How long does it take to build a model? <span class="pm"></span></summary>
        <p>Most architectural models require approximately two to four weeks of production after the scope, design information, and key specifications are confirmed. Larger, highly detailed, illuminated, or technically complex models may require more time. The complete schedule also includes approvals, packaging, transportation, and installation when required.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Where are Carve models built? <span class="pm"></span></summary>
        <p>Client communication and project coordination are handled by our Los Angeles team, with production completed by our established team in China. Scope, approvals, fabrication, quality control, packaging, and delivery remain connected through one coordinated Carve process.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How do you ship the finished model? <span class="pm"></span></summary>
        <p>Packaging is designed around the model's size, fragility, destination, and handling requirements. Depending on the project, this may include protective crating, a fitted transport case, or sectional construction. We coordinate delivery throughout the United States and Canada, with on-site assembly and installation available when required.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How does the quotation process work? <span class="pm"></span></summary>
        <p>Send us your project details, intended use, approximate dimensions, schedule, delivery location, and any available files or references. We review the information and provide a preliminary estimate or identify what is needed to clarify the scope. A formal quotation and proposed timeline are issued once the project requirements are sufficiently defined.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4"><a class="btn btn--ghost svc-all-btn" href="/faq">All FAQs <span class="arrow">→</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>

